; Spells, skills and spheres (read by load_spells() in src/spell_pa.c at boot).
;
; Each entry starts with "#<number> <name>".  The numbers are fixed: the code
; refers to them (SPELL_ARMOR is 51, SKILL_BACKSTAB 1201, see spells.h) and so
; do the skills saved with every character, so never renumber an entry or
; reuse a number.  Spheres are 1-50, spells 51-1200, skills 1201-1700, and
; special abilities from 1701.  A new spell or skill also needs code to make
; it do something; this file only says what it costs, who may use it and how.
; Numbers with no entry are unused.  Lines starting with ';' are comments, and
; the file ends with '$'.
;
;   sphere   <name>        the sphere it belongs to, by the sphere's name
;                          (spheres themselves belong to one of the five
;                          main spheres); a sphere must come before anything
;                          in it
;   percent  <n>           how far into its sphere a character must be to
;                          learn it (default 100)
;   pretime  <n>           rounds of casting before it takes effect
;   mana     <max> <min> <change>
;                          mana at the lowest level, the least it ever costs,
;                          and how much less it costs each level
;   position <pos>         the least the caster must be: dead mortally incap
;                          stunned sleeping resting sitting fighting standing
;                          mounted flying meditating
;   targets  <flags>       ignore char_room char_world fight_self fight_vict
;                          self_only not_self obj_inv obj_room obj_world
;                          obj_equip door must_wield
;   routines <flags>       the magic routines it uses: damage affects
;                          unaffects points alter_objs groups masses areas
;                          summons creations manual
;   violent                it is an attack (not in peaceful rooms, not on
;                          yourself)
;
; Anything left out is 0 (or none).  Names are what players type and see:
; "cast 'cure light wounds'", "practice backstab".

